cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AuditAgent Bench: a benchmark for LLM evaluation of internal control over financial reporting"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it and state which version you used."
type: dataset

# TODO: replace with the legal name to publish under before the first release.
authors:
  - given-names: "TODO"
    family-names: "TODO"
    email: "ajrngn@gmail.com"

repository-code: "https://github.com/TODO/auditagent-bench"
url: "https://auditagent.ca"

abstract: >-
  AuditAgent Bench evaluates how well large language models perform
  internal-control assessment tasks under Section 404 of the Sarbanes-Oxley Act.
  It comprises four tasks: deficiency severity classification and COSO component
  assignment, control design evaluation, clean/deficient discrimination over
  Item 9A disclosures, and standards citation. Items for three of the four tasks
  are derived from material weakness disclosures in SEC EDGAR 10-K filings;
  control design items are synthetic and hand-labeled. Every ground-truth label
  in a released version is human-reviewed. The headline metric is the
  false-positive rate on clean disclosures.

keywords:
  - internal control
  - ICFR
  - SOX 404
  - internal control
  - internal audit
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - COSO
  - SEC EDGAR

license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"

# TODO: set on first release. Version must match the immutable benchmark prefix
# (benchmark/v0.1/), and date-released must be the date that prefix was written.
version: "UNRELEASED"
date-released: "UNKNOWN"
